WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.022
- Everybody has a tuning
fork inside of them,

00:00:05.022 --> 00:00:08.855
and it goes off when you
hit a good golf shot.

00:00:09.784 --> 00:00:13.951
Whether you're blind or
fully sighted, you feel that.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.181
My name is Jeremy Poincenot,

00:00:16.181 --> 00:00:18.931
and I'm the World Blind Golf Champion.

00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:30.051
I'd just turned 19 years old
and was on top of the world,

00:00:30.051 --> 00:00:31.715
and then one day, I was walking on campus,

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:35.043
and I noticed I had to
squint to read a sign.

00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:36.555
Two months later, I'm legally blind

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:38.472
with no central vision.

00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:41.443
This central blur I have is like

00:00:41.443 --> 00:00:44.600
a ghostly, fuzzy static
image in the middle

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.819
that I can't really see anything through.

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:49.483
- He was a great golfer before.

00:00:49.483 --> 00:00:50.765
And, when he lost his vision,

00:00:50.765 --> 00:00:52.579
he thought he'd never play again.

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:53.965
- When my mom told me about blind golf,

00:00:53.965 --> 00:00:55.754
I thought she was cracking a joke.

00:00:55.754 --> 00:00:57.336
But she wasn't kidding.

00:00:57.336 --> 00:00:59.363
I said, we can go to the driving range.

00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:03.446
I'll hit some balls, and
if I miss one, I'm done.

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:06.701
And I didn't miss one.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.704
The tuning fork went off,
and I could feel that was good.

00:01:09.704 --> 00:01:10.704
I like this.

00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:15.604
Golf is an individual sport.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:20.227
Blind golf is very much a team sport.

00:01:20.227 --> 00:01:21.821
- My name is Lionel Poincenot,

00:01:21.821 --> 00:01:23.512
I'm originally from France,

00:01:23.512 --> 00:01:26.243
I'm Jeremy's caddy, coach, guide,

00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:27.243
and his dad.

00:01:29.271 --> 00:01:31.128
- All blind golfers have a guide,

00:01:31.128 --> 00:01:33.453
someone who helps them
out on every single shot.

00:01:33.453 --> 00:01:35.544
The first blind golf
tournament we played in,

00:01:35.544 --> 00:01:37.059
there was a lot of
bickering back and forth

00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:38.360
between my dad and I.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.789
- He would say, well it was your fault,

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:41.086
and it's your fault.

00:01:41.086 --> 00:01:43.156
I mean, it was interesting.

00:01:43.156 --> 00:01:45.123
- I was paired with someone
who was totally blind.

00:01:45.123 --> 00:01:46.573
After the round, I shook his hand

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.896
and I said, “John, it was nice playing with you.”

00:01:48.896 --> 00:01:49.856
And he said,

00:01:49.856 --> 00:01:50.705
"Jeremy, I had a great day today.

00:01:50.705 --> 00:01:52.139
"Thank you."

00:01:52.139 --> 00:01:53.245
And when he said that, I was like, “Oh man.”

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.412
He shot a 324.

00:01:55.892 --> 00:01:56.958
I shot a 97.

00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:58.389
He's happy, I'm not.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:00.501
Who's the real winner here?

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:01.781
I said to my dad, “Let’s

00:02:01.781 --> 00:02:03.772
play more like John Cosolo.”

00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:05.179
- [Lionel] Let's be
happy and enjoy the game.

00:02:05.179 --> 00:02:08.435
So, that's what we do, and it's great.

00:02:08.435 --> 00:02:10.715
- To feel confident going
into a round of golf,

00:02:10.715 --> 00:02:13.381
you want to look good,
you want to feel good,

00:02:13.381 --> 00:02:16.304
and then you hope that
translates to playing good.

00:02:16.304 --> 00:02:17.883
- [Lionel] You know, he
needs to get loose garments

00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:20.507
because you can't swing
with a very tight shirt.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.530
You gotta make sure that he's comfortable

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.259
and that he's got
everything he needs to play.

00:02:23.259 --> 00:02:27.426
Every player and guide, they
have a different process.

00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:30.085
- [Jeremy] He kinda describes the hole.

00:02:30.085 --> 00:02:31.643
- [Lionel] If it's tight, if it's long,

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:33.281
and he sets up to the ball.

00:02:33.281 --> 00:02:34.352
- [Jeremy] And then from behind,

00:02:34.352 --> 00:02:35.821
he looks at how my feet are lined up,

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:36.654
and he tells me to go a little...

00:02:36.654 --> 00:02:37.915
- [Together] More right.

00:02:37.915 --> 00:02:38.832
- Then more left.

00:02:38.832 --> 00:02:39.918
- [Jeremy] I hit the shot,

00:02:39.918 --> 00:02:41.499
then we do that the whole
way around the course.

00:02:41.499 --> 00:02:42.499
- Good putt.

00:02:46.939 --> 00:02:48.796
The first time we went to
the World Championship,

00:02:48.796 --> 00:02:51.163
there was no expectations; it'll be fun,

00:02:51.163 --> 00:02:54.043
then Jeremy got into the playoffs.

00:02:54.043 --> 00:02:56.667
- And I thought, I gotta soak this up.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.928
So I smiled, and I waved to the crowd.

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:02.454
I hit the shot, and it came off perfectly.

00:03:02.454 --> 00:03:05.029
After losing my sight, I felt
like I was living a nightmare.

00:03:05.029 --> 00:03:07.845
And that moment was a total dream.

00:03:07.845 --> 00:03:09.467
And what's especially cool about it

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:13.634
is to be able to share that
experience with my dad.

